cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use quarry in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "quarry: GPU-native spatial queries with incremental updates"
abstract: >-
  A GPU-native spatial query engine that builds BVHs (Karras LBVH or binned SAH) on the
  device and answers ray, closest-point, kNN and radius queries over triangles, point
  clouds and Gaussians. Supports refit and topology edits, and verifies results
  bit-for-bit against a CPU reference.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ycl-berserk"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ycl-berserk/quarry-gpu"
url: "https://github.com/ycl-berserk/quarry-gpu"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-31"
keywords:
  - bvh
  - cuda
  - ray-tracing
  - nearest-neighbor
  - point-cloud
  - gaussian-splatting
  - spatial-index
